WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.768
-My first guest is

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:02.769
a Golden Globe-nominated actor

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:03.903
who's been getting great reviews

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:06.038
for her performance
in the movie "Mank,"

00:00:06.038 --> 00:00:07.773
which is streaming now
on Netflix.

00:00:07.773 --> 00:00:09.475
Here is Amanda Seyfried.

00:00:09.475 --> 00:00:11.377
Ah! Look at -- yeah.

00:00:11.377 --> 00:00:12.912
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:16.282
[ Scat sings ]
I'm so happy you're here.

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:17.784
Love your background,
by the way, too.

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:22.921
[ Knocking ]

00:00:22.921 --> 00:00:25.558
It better be someone I --

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:28.561
-That was an intense knock.

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:33.733
Yeah, go on in and you're
stuck for a minute.

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:36.035
You can go up.

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:37.937
Yeah, no, no, you can go
up here, this way.

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:39.105
-I'm getting nervous.
-Come on in.

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:40.406
Sorry.

00:00:40.406 --> 00:00:42.108
-[ Laughing ]

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:43.476
I'm in a temporary home.

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:44.944
Our dryer is broken.

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:53.052
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.052 --> 00:00:54.620
And there's a chair in front
of the gate [indistinct]

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:57.322
and my husband and daughter --

00:00:57.322 --> 00:00:59.893
-I just got so scared.

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:00.994
Oh, my gosh.

00:01:00.994 --> 00:01:02.261
This is the funniest thing.

00:01:02.261 --> 00:01:03.329
Are you kidding me?

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:04.396
Good.
You have to get that.

00:01:04.396 --> 00:01:05.532
No, you have things to do.

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:07.266
You have things to take care of.

00:01:07.266 --> 00:01:08.935
-But also,
did you hear that knock?

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:10.369
-Frightening.
-It was so aggressive.

00:01:10.369 --> 00:01:12.471
-I felt like I was going
to be interviewed,

00:01:12.471 --> 00:01:13.906
like in
-It was going to be

00:01:13.906 --> 00:01:15.441
-"Dateline."
-a [bleep] SWAT team.

00:01:15.441 --> 00:01:18.344
Yes.
-I thought something
was going down. I go --

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:20.346
I want to talk about "Mank."

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:22.815
Obviously, I have
a thousand questions,

00:01:22.815 --> 00:01:24.651
but I want to get
into this interview

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:27.386
because you posted something
on Instagram recently --

00:01:27.386 --> 00:01:29.455
and that's how I get my news --

00:01:29.455 --> 00:01:32.558
-Same.
-and it is your first
magazine cover.

00:01:32.558 --> 00:01:34.360 line:0%
Can we see this photo?

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.662 line:0%
Now, at first I go,
I kind of --

00:01:36.662 --> 00:01:37.963 line:0%
I didn't understand
what was going on

00:01:37.963 --> 00:01:39.331 line:0%
because it's Clay Aiken.

00:01:39.331 --> 00:01:40.633 line:0%
-Sure. Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:43.402 line:0%
-He's on the cover as well.

00:01:43.402 --> 00:01:45.104 line:0%
-[ Laughing ]
-But right there,

00:01:45.104 --> 00:01:46.672 line:0%
front and center...
-Can we zoom in?

00:01:46.672 --> 00:01:48.607 line:0%
-...whose face do you see?

00:01:48.607 --> 00:01:49.943
Mine.
-Yeah!

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:51.744
[ Clapping ] Aw, come on.
-Look at that cutie.

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:53.612
-How exciting is that, though?
You're on the cover

00:01:53.612 --> 00:01:55.048
of "Entertainment Weekly."
-It was so exciting.

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:57.950
A big deal in our family
and I've never been on it again.

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:00.653
-[ Laughs ]
-Not that I'm sad about it.

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:03.456
It's just -- Yeah.
-Wait for Clay to have
another album

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:05.324
and then we'll start talking.

00:02:05.324 --> 00:02:06.993
-Yeah, okay.
Yeah, no, I didn't think

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:08.194
about that, but that's true.

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:09.762
-You've been on many, many

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:11.096
awesome magazine covers since.

00:02:11.096 --> 00:02:13.500
You've had a great career.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.136
You've been getting rave reviews
for your latest movie, "Mank."

00:02:17.136 --> 00:02:19.338
You got your first
Golden Globe nomination,

00:02:19.338 --> 00:02:21.707
so congrats on that one, buddy.
-Yeah. Thanks.

00:02:21.707 --> 00:02:23.442
Thanks. [ Laughs ]
-How was how was the virtual

00:02:23.442 --> 00:02:26.179
Golden Globe experience?
What was that like?

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:30.016
-Preferable, because I --
-Really?

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:33.719
I could do without the
red carpet hoopla

00:02:33.719 --> 00:02:37.523
because it ends up being
like a cluster eff

00:02:37.523 --> 00:02:39.391
and, as fun as it seems

00:02:39.391 --> 00:02:41.127
and as glamorous as it seemed,
it was really awkward.

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:43.028
You know, it's a pretty
awkward place

00:02:43.028 --> 00:02:45.865
and you're being like thrown
and forced everywhere.

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:49.502
I have my kids on the floor
in front of me --

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:50.903
comfortably --

00:02:50.903 --> 00:02:52.938
while I was sitting there
watching the Globes.

00:02:52.938 --> 00:02:55.574
And I could do things between,
like at commercial breaks.

00:02:55.574 --> 00:02:57.610
It was great.
-Did you get to talk to anyone,

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:02.382
besides your kids?

00:03:02.382 --> 00:03:05.618
-The DP from "Mank" is
in town where we are

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.620
and he's shooting
my husband's movie, actually,

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:10.289
and he came and took pictures
with his wife.

00:03:10.289 --> 00:03:13.059
They're wonderful.
And I talked to Glenn

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:15.694
and all first-name basis,
now, I guess.

00:03:15.694 --> 00:03:17.229
Glenn, Olivia...
-Wow! Oh, so you got to talk

00:03:17.229 --> 00:03:18.998
-...Helena
-to the nominees.

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:20.300
-Jo-- Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:23.202
And I kept seeing Olivia
going like this

00:03:23.202 --> 00:03:25.704
and then I realized
she was asking for the baby.

00:03:25.704 --> 00:03:26.939
[ Laughs ]
-Aw!

00:03:26.939 --> 00:03:30.943
-And so I held the baby
up like --

00:03:30.943 --> 00:03:33.246
Like, you know, in "Lion King."

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:34.781
-[ Laughing ]
-and then I felt like I was

00:03:34.781 --> 00:03:37.016
taking too much time away
from everybody else.

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:38.785
Yeah.
-You crushed it, though,

00:03:38.785 --> 00:03:42.521
You play this Hollywood
actress, Marion Davies,

00:03:42.521 --> 00:03:44.824
and, man, are you stunning
in this movie

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:47.626
and just, you can't take
your eyes off you.

00:03:47.626 --> 00:03:49.695
It was fantastic.

00:03:49.695 --> 00:03:53.032
Did he film that
on regular cameras?

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:54.500
How did you pull that off?

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.835
-It's called David Fincher
and his brain.

00:03:56.835 --> 00:03:58.838
He collects the best
of everybody.

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:01.374
The best production designer,
the best costume designers,

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:02.474
hair and makeup -- everything.

00:04:02.474 --> 00:04:05.311
Everybody is the best
at what they do.

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:07.847
He made an authentic world.

00:04:07.847 --> 00:04:12.352
He recreated the San Simeon.
and I mean, I don't know.

00:04:12.352 --> 00:04:15.220
I was just -- I was very --

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:17.657
I was cast in October

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:19.324
and we started shooting
in November.

00:04:19.324 --> 00:04:22.594
I just had to quickly keep up
with, you know,

00:04:22.594 --> 00:04:25.431
study her and research her
and do as much as I could.

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:27.566
I mean, the script was perfect.
But it was incredible.

00:04:27.566 --> 00:04:30.469
It was so fun to feel
transported every day.

00:04:30.469 --> 00:04:32.504
-Yeah.
-And then walk past the monitor

00:04:32.504 --> 00:04:34.273
and see it's all
black and white.

00:04:34.273 --> 00:04:37.810
What?!
-For people who have not
seen "Mank," yet,

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:40.413
can you tell everyone
what it's about?

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:43.716
-"Mank" is
about Herman J. Mankiewicz,

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:48.120
who wrote the first draft
of "Citizen Kane," which is

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:51.324
-[ Clapping ]
-the greatest movie
ever made, right?

00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:53.392
For a lot of people.
-Yeah.

00:04:53.392 --> 00:04:55.127
-And it's about how he wrote it

00:04:55.127 --> 00:04:56.663
and why he wrote it
and where he was.

00:04:56.663 --> 00:04:59.365
And the backstory
behind "Citizen Kane,"

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:03.335
which is this
big newspaper magnate,

00:05:03.335 --> 00:05:04.770
based
on William Randolph Hearst;

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:07.806
and his wife,
based on Marion Davies,

00:05:07.806 --> 00:05:09.976
inspired by Marion Davies.

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:11.511
They're not the same person.

00:05:11.511 --> 00:05:12.811
-Of course.

00:05:12.811 --> 00:05:15.347
Like it's really great to me
to be able to clarify,

00:05:15.347 --> 00:05:17.249
you know, the difference.

00:05:17.249 --> 00:05:20.987
-It was so fun to watch
and so it didn't --

00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:24.256
You know, I know you've been
on the show so many times.

00:05:24.256 --> 00:05:26.392
It was just great acting.

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:28.427
It was like I was just in --
-Thanks.

00:05:28.427 --> 00:05:30.863
I was like watching
a different person.

00:05:30.863 --> 00:05:33.165
It was amazing.
But it was just beautiful.

00:05:33.165 --> 00:05:34.333
Fun to watch.

00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:36.101
Congrats on all the nominations

00:05:36.101 --> 00:05:38.103
and the awards buzz
you're getting for this.

00:05:38.103 --> 00:05:39.972
I want to show everyone
a clip from the movie.

00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:42.107
Here's Amanda Seyfried
in "Mank."

00:05:42.107 --> 00:05:43.376
Take a look at this.

00:05:43.376 --> 00:05:45.478
-I need a favor, but you're
going to have to promise

00:05:45.478 --> 00:05:47.580
you won't laugh.
-Given the state of the world,

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:48.914
a tall order.
-You're gonna.

00:05:48.914 --> 00:05:49.948
I just know you are.

00:05:49.948 --> 00:05:52.885
-I have got such
a hangover right now,

00:05:52.885 --> 00:05:55.054
there's just a fighting
chance I won't.

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:56.421
-I'm being burned at the stake

00:05:56.421 --> 00:05:58.457
and I am dying for a ciggy-boo.

00:05:58.457 --> 00:05:59.625
[ Laughter ]

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:03.662
There!
God's punishing you.

00:06:03.662 --> 00:06:04.863
Watch those stairs.

00:06:04.863 --> 00:06:06.499
They're treacherous.

00:06:06.499 --> 00:06:08.801
-Every moment of my life
is treacherous.

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:14.006
Any last words?

00:06:14.006 --> 00:06:16.809
-Welcome to San Simeon.

00:06:16.809 --> 00:06:19.044
-I've written worse.
-You've never seen it?

00:06:19.044 --> 00:06:22.415
-No, but George Bernard Shaw
was right.

00:06:22.415 --> 00:06:24.383
-How's that?

00:06:24.383 --> 00:06:27.487
-It's what God might have built,
had he had the money.

00:06:27.487 --> 00:06:29.322
-Well, as they say in the Bronx,

00:06:29.322 --> 00:06:31.590
"Make yourself to home,"
Mr. Mankiewicz.

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:35.060
Or shall I call you Herman?
-No, please call me "Mank."

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:37.029
-Amanda Seyfried, everyone.
When we come back,

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:38.263
Amanda and I are putting

00:06:38.263 --> 00:06:41.234
our singing skills to the test.
Stick around.

